# trial-games.manifest — curated trial-game menu entries layered onto a
# platform card's menu, on top of its machine roster.
#
# Grammar (pipe-delimited; '#' comments; blank lines ignored):
#   trial|<platform>|<label>|<machine>|<asset>|<mount-flag>
#     platform   the platform card this entry appears on (must have a
#                PLATFORM_MACHINES_<platform> roster in host/machines.mk)
#     label      the bootmenu.cfg label — free text, not a machine short
#                name (the menu-loader only displays it; see
#                rapi-bootloader/menu-loader/bootmenu.h)
#     machine    the MAME machine short name this entry boots — an existing
#                roster machine (its own romset ships as usual)
#     asset      the scripts/assets.manifest asset name whose dest is
#                mounted — always under the ruled SD layout
#                (/media/<mediatype>/<driver>/, docs/pi-mame-poc4.html
#                "Trial games" card)
#     mount-flag the MAME media-mount switch prepended to the mounted
#                asset's path (-cass, -flop1, -cart, -quik, …) — MAME's own
#                CLI option for that machine's device instance
#
# Curated by D. (docs/pi-mame-poc4.html "Trial games" card); every asset
# named here is free-tier in scripts/assets.manifest, so an entry is valid
# on both a platform's free and public card (free ⊂ public — see
# scripts/gen-bootmenu.sh's tier doctrine). gen-bootmenu.sh appends one
# extra "label|defaults-string" line per entry after a platform's machine
# roster; scripts/mkcard.sh copies each entry's asset the same way it
# copies a roster machine's MACHINE_ASSETS_* media. No new card mechanism:
# same bootmenu.cfg format, same menu-loader, same defaults-block ABI.
#
# -flop8 (the c64 entries) is BEST-EFFORT: the C64 attaches its floppy
# drive over the IEC bus at device address 8, and this project has no MAME
# binary to execute (bare-metal cross-compiled target) to confirm the
# switch against `-listmedia`. Verify before treating those five entries
# as proven.

